{% comment %}
  Step 1 of 5 — "Choose your concern". New step inserted between Entry and
  Doctor Select: after choosing "Book a consultation" on Entry, the visitor
  picks a concern here first, THEN moves on to picking a doctor.
  Explicit instruction: this only applies to the consultation path — Therapy
  Slot's flow is untouched.

  Inserting this as step 1 pushed every downstream step's progress
  dots/label down by one (Doctor Select 1/5->2/5, Slot Picker 2/5->3/5,
  Patient Details 3/5->4/5) — Confirmation was already 5/5 (last of 5) so it
  needed no change. See kal-booking-flow.js's goToStep comment / each step's
  own header for the renumbering.

  This step is a structured replacement for a free-text "what are you
  coming in for" field, not a doctor filter/search — so each row is just an
  icon + name + checkbox, no doctor count. Selecting a concern doesn't
  filter the Doctor Select list that follows; it still shows its same
  doctor list regardless of what's picked here.

  MOBILE REDESIGN (this file, this pass): a new Figma spec replaced the
  original single-select/radio version with:
  - Multi-select checkboxes instead of a single radio (see
    kal-booking-flow-concern-row.liquid and kal-booking-flow.js's
    concernSelect Set)
  - A new, larger category list (General Wellness, Bone/Joint/Muscle Pain,
    Gut Health, PCOS/PCOD/Menopause, Skin/Hair, Diabetes/Thyroid/BP,
    Reproductive Health/Infertility, Liver/Kidney Health, Sleep/General
    Lifestyle, Respiratory/General Immunity, Other) replacing the old
    medical-specialty names
  - The "Not sure?" banner moved from the footer to right under the title
  - A location badge (facility name only, no working dropdown — explicit
    instruction: "for now dont need this dropdown just the selected
    facility should be shown here") in place of the progress dots in the
    mobile header, with a separate "STEP 1 OF 5 / Next: Mode & Doctor" bar
    + progress bar underneath
  - A floating down-chevron scroll hint over the list

  Explicit instruction: THIS PASS IS MOBILE-ONLY. The desktop composition
  (progress dots in the header, no step-bar, no scroll hint) is
  deliberately left exactly as it was — every new element below is hidden
  at 750px+, and the pre-existing desktop elements are hidden below 750px
  instead of removed. See kal-booking-flow.css's own comment on this
  step for exactly which classes do which.

  ICONS (updated to match a later Figma pass): each of the 11 concerns now
  has its own dedicated 'concern-*' icon in kal-booking-icons.liquid,
  exported directly from that spec — the earlier pass's reused/placeholder
  icons (orthopedics standing in for Bone/Joint/Muscle Pain, etc.) have
  been replaced. The old sprite-sheet specialty icons ('concern-general-
  medicine', 'concern-orthopedics', etc.) are left in kal-booking-icons.liquid
  unused by this step in case another step still wants them.

  Each row is also now a bordered card (border/radius/padding on
  .kal-concern-row) per the updated spec, rather than a plain borderless
  row — see kal-booking-flow.css's own comment on this step.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — see the "SHARED
  STEP SHELL" comment in kal-booking-flow.css for why and how the layout
  switches at 750px.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-concern-select kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Choose your concern</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
        We&rsquo;ll match you with available doctors. Book a consultation
        in under a minute in-clinic or video.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'entry', step_number: 1, step_total: 5, next_label: 'Mode & Doctor', location_switchable: true -%}

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Choose your concern</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__banner">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--search">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'search' -%}
        </span>
        <span class="kal-concern-select__banner-text">Not sure? <strong>General Wellness</strong> will guide you from there.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__list">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-general-wellness', name: 'General Wellness', concern_key: 'general-wellness', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-bone-joint-muscle', name: 'Bone, Joint, Muscle Pain', concern_key: 'bone-joint-muscle-pain', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-gut-health', name: 'Gut Health', concern_key: 'gut-health', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-pcos-pcod-menopause', name: 'PCOS, PCOD, Menopause', concern_key: 'pcos-pcod-menopause', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-skin-hair', name: 'Skin, Hair', concern_key: 'skin-hair', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-diabetes-thyroid-bp', name: 'Diabetes, Thyroid, BP', concern_key: 'diabetes-thyroid-bp', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-reproductive-health', name: 'Reproductive Health, Infertility', concern_key: 'reproductive-health-infertility', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-liver-kidney', name: 'Liver, Kidney Health', concern_key: 'liver-kidney-health', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-sleep-lifestyle', name: 'Sleep, General Lifestyle', concern_key: 'sleep-general-lifestyle', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-respiratory-immunity', name: 'Respiratory, General Immunity', concern_key: 'respiratory-general-immunity', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-other', name: 'Other', concern_key: 'other', selected: false -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Mobile-only floating scroll hint — signals more concerns below AND
      scrolls the list down a page when clicked (see
      data-kal-scroll-hint's click handler in kal-booking-flow.js).
      Positioned relative to the panel so it stays fixed near the bottom
      regardless of scroll position. Hidden at 750px+, see CSS.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="kal-concern-select__scroll-hint" data-kal-scroll-hint aria-label="Scroll down">
      {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-right' -%}
    </button>

    {%- comment -%}
      Per the updated Figma spec, this footer isn't just a disabled button
      sitting there from the start — it doesn't exist at all until the
      visitor has picked at least one concern (see kal-booking-flow.js's
      updateConcernContinueButton, which toggles the `hidden` attribute on
      data-kal-concern-footer, not just the button's `disabled` state).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer" data-kal-concern-footer hidden>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="doctor-select" data-kal-concern-continue>
        Continue
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
